  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The machine file can state a new optional key, `tooling.max_tool_number`. It is the highest tool number that the control's tool table holds.\n- The machine reader and the raw post engine refuse a value that is not a whole number of 1 or more. The message names the key.\n- The key is an installation fact, the same as `tooling.tool_change`. The mirror carries it. Scripts read it as `machine.toolNumberMax`.\n- `fehlmann-picomax55.mch` states `\"max_tool_number\": 254`.\n- `heidenhain-klartext.cps` refuses a higher tool number with a script error.\n- `heidenhain.cps` refuses a higher tool number with a counted warning. It refuses a spindle speed above the machine maximum in the same way.\n- A machine without the key keeps the old behaviour. Klartext keeps its limit of 32767. DIN/ISO has no limit.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/4087-tool-table-max.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe Picomax tool table has 254 lines (MP 7260 = 254, and the programming manual p. 2-16). No machine fact carried this limit. The Klartext post accepted tool numbers up to 32767, and the DIN/ISO post accepted all tool numbers. A program with tool 255 posted, and then the control stopped it with an alarm.\n\n`tooling.number_of_tools` is a different fact. It counts the distinct tools in a changer (`check_tool_count`). It does not limit the tool number.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, in `crates/post/tests/machine_controller.rs`:\n\n- `heidenhain_posts_refuse_a_tool_number_above_the_machine_tool_table`. Both posts run on the Picomax, with the raw file and with the parsed mirror. Tool 254 posts. Tool 255 is refused with a message that names the tool number and the tool table.\n- `malformed_declared_facts_refuse_at_the_machine_reader_and_raw_engine`. Four new bad values: 0, -1, 25.5 and `\"254\"`.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On unchanged code, tool 255 posted through `heidenhain.cps` with no message, and value 0 was accepted.\n\nMutations. For each one, I put back the code and ran the pins:\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `heidenhain-klartext.cps` from upstream/main | red (`heidenhain-klartext.cps:` no refusal) |\n| `heidenhain.cps` from upstream/main | red (`heidenhain.cps:` no refusal) |\n| `post/machine_installation.rs` without the mirror and script property | red |\n| the `n >= 1` guard removed from `max_tool_number` | red (value 0 accepted) |\n| restored | green, 6 of 6 |\n\nGates on the final code tree (head `ff8931308`; the quick gate ran before the decision file was committed, with the same code):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 341 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. These steps are included:\n  - `example_catalog` (43 passed)\n  - `example_catalog_adaptive`\n  - `example_catalog_edge_work`\n  - `golden_cl`\n  - `conformance`\n  - `klartext_builtin`\n  - `script_heidenhain` and `script_heidenhain_klartext`\n  - the machine suites of `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-post`\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reaches 72 steps, which is the whole app heavy lane. This is a P3 PR. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a heavy step only to a P1 PR under the safety floor.\n\nBuild note: the shared sccache server does not complete compile requests on this machine. A quick gate with the cache stalled in the build step (STALL row). I ran all gates and tests with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` and without `RUSTC_WRAPPER`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The quick gate ran the example catalog, `golden_cl`, `conformance` and the recorded script suites of both Heidenhain posts. No golden file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The machine sheet and the machine editor do not show the new key. The app does not judge the key in its own validator (`crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs`). The reader refuses a bad value when the file loads.\n- I did not do an end-to-end check in the app GUI. The app posts through the same mirror that the pin uses.\n- No other machine file states the key.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #4114 changes `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps` and `assets/posts/heidenhain-klartext.cps`. It changes other functions: the manifest line and a new `manualChange`. It does not change `onToolChange`. This PR adds lines at the start of `onToolChange` in `heidenhain.cps`, near the comment that #4114 changes. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: The machine file can state the highest tool number of the tool table (`tooling.max_tool_number`); the Fehlmann Picomax 55 states 254, and both Heidenhain posts refuse a higher tool number by name.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4087\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
